Modified 2026-11-02 by PRP contributors.
The only behavioral change is getCurrentPeerConnectionIdLength() in
tech/kwik/core/cid/ConnectionIdManager.java. A valid zero-length peer connection
ID is represented by a null peer registry; the getter now returns zero in that
state rather than dereferencing it. The peer-selected connection ID is unchanged.
The stream-send scheduling fix is included unchanged from official Kwik 0.12.1.
No application-specific behavior, reflection, retry policy, or wire change is added.

